  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Romania First Fiscal and Growth DPL</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Project Development Objective (PDO) is to support the Government of Romania in strengthening resilience by :i) restoring fiscal sustainability; and ii) enabling private sector-led growth.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The development objective of the First Fiscal and Growth Development Policy Loan Program for Romania is to support the Government of Romania in strengthening resilience by :(i) restoring fiscal sustainability; and (ii) enabling private sector-led growth. The policy matrix addresses Romania&apos;s interconnected fiscal and economic challenges through two complementary pillars, balancing the urgent need for a major fiscal sustainability effort through tax and spending reforms (Pillar 1), while fostering private sector-led growth by expanding access to finance, promoting innovation, and mobilizing private investment to boost competitiveness and job creation (pillar 2). Through these pillars, the operation also supports Romania&apos;s efforts to strengthen resilience and adaptive capacity by: (i) reinforcing fiscal sustainability, (ii) facilitating investments to diversify Romania&apos;s energy mix, (iii) improving risk management frameworks, and (iv) creating space for climate adaptation investments.</narrative>
  </description>
